
PORT=3001

# Single PostgreSQL database for all data
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://pomodoro:pomodoro@localhost:5432/pomodoro

# JWT secrets (min 32 chars)
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-to-a-random-32-char-string!!
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-to-another-random-32-char!!

# Timer defaults (optional)
DEFAULT_FOCUS_MINUTES=25
DEFAULT_SHORT_BREAK_MINUTES=5
DEFAULT_LONG_BREAK_MINUTES=15

# Expo push notifications (optional until configured)

# Encrypts third-party OAuth tokens at rest (currently Google Calendar access
# and refresh tokens in external_calendar_connections). OPTIONAL: unset, the
# server boots normally and those tokens are stored as they always were, so
# adding this cannot break a deploy.
#
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Setting it later is safe and needs no migration. `open()` passes plaintext
# through untouched, so existing rows keep working, and each connection is
# re-written encrypted the next time its access token is refreshed.
# Losing the key after rows are sealed means those users must reconnect Google.
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ─── Transactional email (password reset) ────────────────────────────────────
# All OPTIONAL. Unset, sending is a logged no-op and the server boots normally,
# so a deploy without these cannot 500 the password-reset route — it just does
# not deliver. See src/lib/email.ts.
#
# Plain SMTP, so any provider works and switching is a config change, not a code
# change. NO DOMAIN IS REQUIRED if you use a provider that offers single-sender
# verification: you verify one address you already own and send from it.
#
# Brevo, for example (300 emails/day free, no card):
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=<the login Brevo shows on its SMTP page, not your account email>
#   SMTP_PASS=<the SMTP key Brevo generates>
#   EMAIL_FROM=Ascend <the-address-you-verified@example.com>
#
# Port matters: 587 is STARTTLS, 465 is implicit TLS. src/lib/email.ts picks the
# mode from the port, so getting it wrong fails as a timeout with no useful error.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# EMAIL_FROM=
